🔥 Lambda Function in Kotlin (Android)

✅ Definition

A Lambda function is an anonymous function (a function without a name) that can be:

Stored in a variable
Passed as a parameter
Returned from another function

In Kotlin, lambdas are heavily used because Kotlin is a functional + object-oriented language.

✅ When To Use Lambda Function in Kotlin (Android)
**************************************************
You use a Lambda when:
You want to pass behavior (logic) as a parameter instead of hardcoding it.

******************************************************************************************************************

Syntax For Writing Lambda function in a method.

fun demoExample ( param1: Type1, param2: Type1 , operation: (param3 : InputType, param4 : InputType) -> ReturnType ) {
            // Business Logic
}

demoExample --> Function Name
param1: Type1,param2: Type1 , operation: (InputType, InputType) -> ReturnType    ----> demoExample takes 3 parameter

param1: Type1,param2: Type1   ---> 2 Normal Parameter
operation: (InputType, InputType) -> ReturnType  -----> 1 Lambda function

operation: (InputType, InputType) -> ReturnType
 operation--> Method Name
 (InputType, InputType) ---> Takes 2 parameter
 ReturnType ---> Method is having a return type.

